# Build context for ci/Dockerfile.ci and ci/Dockerfile.local-test (both use the
# repo root as context; the dev container has its own .dockerignore because its
# context is .devcontainer/).
#
# Filled-in env files are kept out: ci/Dockerfile.local-test does `COPY ci ci/`,
# which would otherwise bake ci/.env.local's secrets into an image layer.
# Nothing in the image reads them anyway — ci/fill-envs.sh generates the .env
# files at runtime from the environment `docker run --env-file` injects.
#
# The .example templates are kept (ci/check-envs.sh parses one), and so are the
# ci/env-templates/*.env files, whose names don't start with `.env`.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env*.example
